#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` - delete unreachable [store objects](../store/store-"
"object.md)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` \\[`--delete-old`\\] \\[`-d`\\] \\[`--delete-older-"
"than` _period_\\] \\[`--max-freed` _bytes_\\] \\[`--dry-run`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:9
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:11
msgid ""
"The command `nix-collect-garbage` is mostly an alias of [`nix-store --gc`]"
"(../command-ref/nix-store/gc.md). That is, it deletes all unreachable [store "
"objects](../store/store-object.md) in the Nix store to clean up your system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:14
msgid ""
"However, it provides two additional options, [`--delete-old`](#opt-delete-"
"old) and [`--delete-older-than`](#opt-delete-older-than), which also delete "
"old [profiles](../command-ref/files/profiles.md), allowing potentially more "
"[store objects](../store/store-object.md) to be deleted because profiles are "
"also garbage collection roots. These options are the equivalent of running "
"[`nix-env --delete-generations`](../command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations."
"md) with various augments on multiple profiles, prior to running `nix-"
"collect-garbage` (or just `nix-store --gc`) without any flags."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:22
#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:304
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:24
msgid "Deleting previous configurations makes rollbacks to them impossible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:26
msgid ""
"These flags should be used with care, because they potentially delete "
"generations of profiles used by other users on the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:28
msgid "Locations searched for profiles"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:30
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` cannot know about all profiles; that information "
"doesn't exist. Instead, it looks in a few locations, and acts on all "
"profiles it finds there:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:33
msgid ""
"The default profile locations as specified in the [profiles](../command-ref/"
"files/profiles.md) section of the manual."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:35
msgid "**NOTE**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:37
msgid "Not stable; subject to change"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:39
msgid ""
"Do not rely on this functionality; it just exists for migration purposes and "
"may change in the future. These deprecated paths remain a private "
"implementation detail of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:42
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles` and `$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:44
msgid ""
"With the exception of `$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root` and "
"`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/default`, these directories are no longer used by "
"other commands. `nix-collect-garbage` looks there anyways in order to clean "
"up profiles from older versions of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:47
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:49
msgid ""
"These options are for deleting old [profiles](../command-ref/files/profiles."
"md) prior to deleting unreachable [store objects](../store/store-object.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:51
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-delete-old\">[`--delete-old`](#opt-delete-old)</span> / `-d`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:53
msgid "Delete all old generations of profiles."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:55
msgid ""
"This is the equivalent of invoking [`nix-env --delete-generations old`](../"
"command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md#generations-old) on each found "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:57
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-delete-older-than\">[`--delete-older-than`](#opt-delete-older-"
"than)</span> _period_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:59
msgid ""
"Delete all generations of profiles older than the specified amount (except "
"for the generations that were active at that point in time). _period_ is a "
"value such as `30d`, which would mean 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:62
msgid ""
"This is the equivalent of invoking [`nix-env --delete-generations <period>`]"
"(../command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md#generations-time) on each "
"found profile. See the documentation of that command for additional "
"information about the _period_ argument."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:65
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-freed\">[`--max-freed`](#opt-max-freed)</span> _bytes_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:69
msgid ""
"Keep deleting paths until at least _bytes_ bytes have been deleted, then "
"stop. The argument _bytes_ can be followed by the multiplicative suffix `K`, "
"`M`, `G` or `T`, denoting KiB, MiB, GiB or TiB units."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:78
msgid "Common Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:80
msgid "Most Nix commands accept the following command-line options:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:82
msgid "<span id=\"opt-help\">[`--help`](#opt-help)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:84
msgid "Prints out a summary of the command syntax and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:86
msgid "<span id=\"opt-version\">[`--version`](#opt-version)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:88
msgid "Prints out the Nix version number on standard output and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:90
msgid ""
"For machine-readable output, including versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against, see the [`nix version`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md) "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:93
msgid "<span id=\"opt-verbose\">[`--verbose`](#opt-verbose)</span> / `-v`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:95
msgid ""
"Increases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. For each Nix operation, the information printed on standard output is "
"well-defined; any diagnostic information is printed on standard error, never "
"on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:99
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. Currently, the following verbosity "
"levels exist:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:102
msgid "`0` “Errors only”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:104
msgid "Only print messages explaining why the Nix invocation failed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:106
msgid "`1` “Informational”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:108
msgid "Print _useful_ messages about what Nix is doing. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:111
msgid "`2` “Talkative”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:113
msgid "Print more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:115
msgid "`3` “Chatty”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:117
msgid "Print even more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:119
msgid "`4` “Debug”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:121
msgid "Print debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:123
msgid "`5` “Vomit”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:125
msgid "Print vast amounts of debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:127
msgid "<span id=\"opt-quiet\">[`--quiet`](#opt-quiet)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:129
msgid ""
"Decreases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. This is the inverse option to `-v` / `--verbose`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:132
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. See the previous verbosity levels "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:135
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-log-format\">[`--log-format`](#opt-log-format)</span> _format_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:137
msgid ""
"This option can be used to change the output of the log format, with "
"_format_ being one of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:139
msgid "`raw`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:141
msgid "This is the raw format, as outputted by nix-build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:143
msgid "`internal-json`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:145
msgid "Outputs the logs in a structured manner."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:147
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:149
msgid ""
"While the schema itself is relatively stable, the format of the error-"
"messages (namely of the `msg`\\-field) can change between releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:153
msgid "`bar`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:155
msgid "Only display a progress bar during the builds."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:157
msgid "`bar-with-logs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:159
msgid "Display the raw logs, with the progress bar at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:161
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-no-build-output\">[`--no-build-output`](#opt-no-build-"
"output)</span> / `-Q`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:163
msgid ""
"By default, output written by builders to standard output and standard error "
"is echoed to the Nix command's standard error. This option suppresses this "
"behaviour. Note that the builder's standard output and error are always "
"written to a log file in `prefix/nix/var/log/nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:167
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-jobs\">[`--max-jobs`](#opt-max-jobs)</span> / `-j` "
"_number_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:169
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of build jobs that Nix will perform in parallel to "
"the specified number. Specify `auto` to use the number of CPUs in the "
"system. The default is specified by the `max-jobs` configuration setting, "
"which itself defaults to `1`. A higher value is useful on SMP systems or to "
"exploit I/O latency."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:174
msgid ""
"Setting it to `0` disallows building on the local machine, which is useful "
"when you want builds to happen only on remote builders."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:176
msgid "<span id=\"opt-cores\">[`--cores`](#opt-cores)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:178
msgid ""
"Sets the value of the `NIX_BUILD_CORES` environment variable in the "
"invocation of builders. Builders can use this variable at their discretion "
"to control the maximum amount of parallelism. For instance, in Nixpkgs, if "
"the derivation attribute `enableParallelBuilding` is set to `true`, the "
"builder passes the `-jN` flag to GNU Make. It defaults to the value of the "
"`cores` configuration setting, if set, or `1` otherwise. The value `0` means "
"that the builder should use all available CPU cores in the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:184
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-silent-time\">[`--max-silent-time`](#opt-max-silent-"
"time)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:186
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can go without producing "
"any data on standard output or standard error. The default is specified by "
"the `max-silent-time` configuration setting. `0` means no time-out."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:190
msgid "<span id=\"opt-timeout\">[`--timeout`](#opt-timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:192
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can run. The default is "
"specified by the `timeout` configuration setting. `0` means no timeout."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:196
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-going\">[`--keep-going`](#opt-keep-going)</span> / `-k`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:198
msgid ""
"Keep going in case of failed builds, to the greatest extent possible. That "
"is, if building an input of some derivation fails, Nix will still build the "
"other inputs, but not the derivation itself. Without this option, Nix stops "
"if any build fails (except for builds of substitutes), possibly killing "
"builds in progress (in case of parallel or distributed builds)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:202
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-failed\">[`--keep-failed`](#opt-keep-failed)</span> / `-"
"K`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:204
msgid ""
"Specifies that in case of a build failure, the temporary directory (usually "
"in `/tmp`) in which the build takes place should not be deleted. The path of "
"the build directory is printed as an informational message."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:207
msgid "<span id=\"opt-fallback\">[`--fallback`](#opt-fallback)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:209
msgid ""
"Whenever Nix attempts to build a derivation for which substitutes are known "
"for each output path, but realising the output paths through the substitutes "
"fails, fall back on building the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:211
msgid ""
"The most common scenario in which this is useful is when we have registered "
"substitutes in order to perform binary distribution from, say, a network "
"repository. If the repository is down, the realisation of the derivation "
"will fail. When this option is specified, Nix will build the derivation "
"instead. Thus, installation from binaries falls back on installation from "
"source. This option is not the default since it is generally not desirable "
"for a transient failure in obtaining the substitutes to lead to a full build "
"from source (with the related consumption of resources)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:217
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-readonly-mode\">[`--readonly-mode`](#opt-readonly-mode)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:219
msgid ""
"When this option is used, no attempt is made to open the Nix database. Most "
"Nix operations do need database access, so those operations will fail."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:222
msgid "<span id=\"opt-arg\">[`--arg`](#opt-arg)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:224
msgid ""
"This option is accepted by `nix-env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-shell` and "
"`nix-build`. When evaluating Nix expressions, the expression evaluator will "
"automatically try to call functions that it encounters. It can automatically "
"call functions for which every argument has a [default value](../language/"
"syntax.md#functions) (e.g., `{ argName ?  defaultValue }: ...`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:228
msgid ""
"With `--arg`, you can also call functions that have arguments without a "
"default value (or override a default value). That is, if the evaluator "
"encounters a function with an argument named _name_, it will call it with "
"value _value_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:231
msgid ""
"For instance, the top-level `default.nix` in Nixpkgs is actually a function:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:240
msgid ""
"So if you call this Nix expression (e.g., when you do `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname`), the function will be called automatically using the value "
"[`builtins.currentSystem`](../language/builtins.md) for the `system` "
"argument. You can override this using `--arg`, e.g., `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname --arg system \\\"i686-freebsd\\\"`. (Note that since the "
"argument is a Nix string literal, you have to escape the quotes.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:244
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-file\">[`--arg-from-file`](#opt-arg-from-file)</"
"span> _name_ _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:246
msgid ""
"Pass the contents of file _path_ as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:248
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-stdin\">[`--arg-from-stdin`](#opt-arg-from-stdin)</"
"span> _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:250
msgid "Pass the contents of stdin as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:252
msgid "<span id=\"opt-argstr\">[`--argstr`](#opt-argstr)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:254
msgid ""
"This option is like `--arg`, only the value is not a Nix expression but a "
"string. So instead of `--arg system \\\"i686-linux\\\"` (the outer quotes "
"are to keep the shell happy) you can say `--argstr system i686-linux`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:257
msgid "<span id=\"opt-attr\">[`--attr`](#opt-attr)</span> / `-A` _attrPath_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:259
msgid ""
"Select an attribute from the top-level Nix expression being evaluated. (`nix-"
"env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.) The _attribute "
"path_ _attrPath_ is a sequence of attribute names separated by dots. For "
"instance, given a top-level Nix expression _e_, the attribute path `xorg."
"xorgserver` would cause the expression `e.xorg.xorgserver` to be used. See "
"[`nix-env --install`](../command-ref/nix-env/install.md) for some concrete "
"examples."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:265
msgid ""
"In addition to attribute names, you can also specify array indices. For "
"instance, the attribute path `foo.3.bar` selects the `bar` attribute of the "
"fourth element of the array in the `foo` attribute of the top-level "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:270
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-eval-store\">[`--eval-store`](#opt-eval-store)</span> _store-"
"url_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:272
msgid ""
"The [URL to the Nix store](../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to use "
"for evaluation, i.e. where to store derivations (`.drv` files) and inputs "
"referenced by them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:274
msgid "<span id=\"opt-expr\">[`--expr`](#opt-expr)</span> / `-E`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:276
msgid ""
"Interpret the command line arguments as a list of Nix expressions to be "
"parsed and evaluated, rather than as a list of file names of Nix "
"expressions. (`nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:279
msgid ""
"For `nix-shell`, this option is commonly used to give you a shell in which "
"you can build the packages returned by the expression. If you want to get a "
"shell which contain the _built_ packages ready for use, give your expression "
"to the `nix-shell --packages ` convenience flag instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:282
msgid "<span id=\"opt-I\">[`-I` / `--include`](#opt-I)</span> _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:284
msgid ""
"Add an entry to the list of search paths used to resolve [lookup paths](../"
"language/constructs/lookup-path.md). This option may be given multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:287
msgid ""
"Paths added through `-I` take precedence over the [`nix-path` configuration "
"setting](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-nix-path) and the [`NIX_PATH` "
"environment variable](../command-ref/env-common.md#env-NIX_PATH)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:289
msgid "<span id=\"opt-impure\">[`--impure`](#opt-impure)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:291
msgid "Allow access to mutable paths and repositories."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:293
msgid "<span id=\"opt-option\">[`--option`](#opt-option)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:295
msgid ""
"Set the Nix configuration option _name_ to _value_. This overrides settings "
"in the Nix configuration file (see nix.conf5)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:298
msgid "<span id=\"opt-repair\">[`--repair`](#opt-repair)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:300
msgid ""
"Fix corrupted or missing store paths by redownloading or rebuilding them. "
"Note that this is slow because it requires computing a cryptographic hash of "
"the contents of every path in the closure of the build. Also note the "
"warning under `nix-store --repair-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:306
msgid ""
"See [`man nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#command-line-flags) for "
"overriding configuration settings with command line flags."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:309
msgid "Common Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:311
msgid "Most Nix commands interpret the following environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:313
msgid "Configuration environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:315
msgid ""
"The following environment variables affect how Nix loads its configuration. "
"See the [configuration file](../command-ref/conf-file.md#configuration-file) "
"documentation for full details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:318
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_CONF_DIR\">[`NIX_CONF_DIR`](#env-NIX_CONF_DIR)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:320
msgid "Overrides the system configuration directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:322
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_USER_CONF_FILES\">[`NIX_USER_CONF_FILES`](#env-"
"NIX_USER_CONF_FILES)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:324
msgid "Overrides the user configuration file locations."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:326
msgid "<span id=\"env-NIX_CONFIG\">[`NIX_CONFIG`](#env-NIX_CONFIG)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:328
msgid "Provides configuration settings inline."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:330
msgid "Store setting environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:332
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE\">[`NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE`](#env-"
"NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:334
msgid ""
"Normally, the Nix store directory (typically `/nix/store`) is not allowed to "
"contain any symlink components. This is to prevent “impure” builds. Builders "
"sometimes “canonicalise” paths by resolving all symlink components. Thus, "
"builds on different machines (with `/nix/store` resolving to different "
"locations) could yield different results. This is generally not a problem, "
"except when builds are deployed to machines where `/nix/store` resolves "
"differently. If you are sure that you’re not going to do that, you can set "
"`NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE` to `1`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:344
msgid ""
